1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,737
The strategy in this report is
to move beyond competing on

2
00:00:03,791 --> 00:00:07,090
size and focus on showing parents
why they should choose JEI.

3
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:12,060
We identified three key challenges
facing the traditional workbook market.

4
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:15,089
First, as learning becomes
increasingly digital,

5
00:00:15,142 --> 00:00:17,560
more EdTech products
have entered the market.

6
00:00:18,010 --> 00:00:20,962
However, parents are becoming
more concerned about whether

7
00:00:21,013 --> 00:00:23,660
these products deliver
meaningful learning benefits.

8
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:28,450
Second, instructors face significant
pressure to attract new customers.

9
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:31,994
This leads to increased stress
and high instructor turnover,

10
00:00:32,046 --> 00:00:35,450
creating a continuing cycle of
instructors leaving the profession.

11
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:39,902
Third, broad messages such as
“Self-Learning” and “The Ability to Learn

12
00:00:39,959 --> 00:00:44,130
Independently” have not given parents
a clear enough reason to choose JEI.

13
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:48,840
JEI must address two strategic enemies.

14
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:52,880
The first is repeating basic math
calculations without thinking.

15
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:55,948
This can make it hard for
students to solve written math

16
00:00:55,995 --> 00:00:58,940
problems in higher grades and may
lead them to give up on math.

17
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,920
The second is mindless tablet tapping.

18
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:05,256
Without clear learning support
or instructor coaching,

19
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:08,410
simply using tablets does not
show real learning benefits.

20
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:14,740
We propose that JEI move beyond traditional
workbooks and repetitive math drills.

21
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:18,861
Through precise assessment, we can
identify learning gaps and help

22
00:01:18,917 --> 00:01:22,810
children understand basic principles
and solve problems independently.

23
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:26,330
Our goal is to establish
true self-directed learning.

24
00:01:27,030 --> 00:01:30,580
Our Verbal Nail is “A Child Who
Knows Why They Got an Answer Wrong.”

25
00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:33,830
This message speaks directly
to parents’ concerns.

26
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:37,328
Our Visual Hammer is the “Defect
Linker,” a visual map that

27
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:40,480
connects learning gaps across
different learning objectives.

28
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:45,300
With a single visual, we can build parents’
trust without lengthy explanations.

29
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,980
Our proposed brand slogan is “Find
the Way, Not Just the Answer.”

30
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:53,765
Rather than simply giving children
the right answers, JEI helps

31
00:01:53,818 --> 00:01:57,470
them understand the basic principles
and find solutions on their own.

32
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:01,060
There are also two risks to consider.

33
00:02:01,510 --> 00:02:04,980
A more focused message may appeal
to a smaller group of parents.

34
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:08,811
Also, learning gaps may be harder
to show clearly for preschool

35
00:02:08,865 --> 00:02:11,870
and younger elementary students
than for older students.

36
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:16,480
We will simplify our product
lineup into three stages.

37
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:21,650
Stage One offers a free, precise mobile
assessment to attract potential customers.

38
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:26,850
Stage Two builds foundational skills
through JEI Math, Korean, and Hangul.

39
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:30,055
Stage Three expands our
offerings through Thinking

40
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:32,480
PIZZA and school exam
preparation packages.

41
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:36,253
This will encourage enrollment
in multiple subjects, increase

42
00:02:36,308 --> 00:02:39,250
revenue per customer, and
support long-term retention.

43
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:42,460
We will focus on two core target groups.

44
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:45,920
The first is children preparing
for elementary school.

45
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:49,098
We will offer precise
school-readiness assessments

46
00:02:49,153 --> 00:02:51,990
and six learning courses,
including Math and Hangul.

47
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,178
These programs will help
children build foundational

48
00:02:55,231 --> 00:02:57,390
skills before entering elementary school.

49
00:02:58,090 --> 00:03:00,530
Second, students in Grades 1 to 3.

50
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:04,226
We will use a 10-minute
diagnostic assessment to identify

51
00:03:04,283 --> 00:03:07,530
learning gaps and connect
students with JEI Math, Korean,

52
00:03:07,587 --> 00:03:10,890
and Thinking PIZZA, our signature
Thinking Skills program.

53
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:13,661
We will then support
continued learning through

54
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:16,130
higher grades and middle
school exam preparation.

55
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:20,710
Our first step is to launch a
free mobile assessment tool.

56
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:25,430
Parents will be able to identify their
child’s learning gaps in about 10 minutes.

57
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:30,730
This will lower the barrier to trying
JEI and help us attract new customers.

58
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:35,730
Second, we will standardize instructor
consultations and coaching messages.

59
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,494
When parents are concerned that
their child is falling behind,

60
00:03:39,548 --> 00:03:42,969
instructors will use a consistent
message: “Moving ahead without

61
00:03:43,022 --> 00:03:46,550
fixing learning gaps can cause
serious problems in higher grades.”

62
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,230
This helps parents understand why
addressing learning gaps is important.

63
00:03:51,930 --> 00:03:54,781
Third, we will develop
grading support tools with

64
00:03:54,839 --> 00:03:57,690
the goal of reducing routine
grading work by 50%.

65
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:02,153
This will help reduce instructors’
administrative and sales-related burdens,

66
00:04:02,206 --> 00:04:05,850
allowing them to focus more on
learning coaching and student support.

67
00:04:06,550 --> 00:04:08,952
Fourth, every Friday,
we will send parents a

68
00:04:09,006 --> 00:04:11,790
visual progress report
through KakaoTalk Messenger.

69
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:14,862
The report will show how
each child's learning gaps

70
00:04:14,914 --> 00:04:17,690
are being addressed and what
progress they are making.

71
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,840
This will help build parent trust
and improve parent satisfaction.

72
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:25,060
At the same time, our early-warning system

73
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:27,880
will help identify students
who may leave JEI.

74
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:31,456
Before parents decide to withdraw
their children, instructors

75
00:04:31,507 --> 00:04:34,940
will proactively offer solutions
to encourage continued enrollment.

76
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:40,110
This concludes the summary of our brand
repositioning and execution strategy.

77
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,290
Thank you.

